.TH PQBLOCKS_HYBRID 3 "2026-09-17" "pqblocks 1.0.0" "PQBlocks C API Manual"
.SH NAME
pqblocks_hybrid \- Post-Quantum and Classical Hybrid Key Encapsulation and Signatures
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <pqblocks_kem.h>
.B #include <pqblocks_sig.h>
.PP
.BI "PQBLOCKS_KEM_X25519_MLKEM768 *PQBLOCKS_KEM_X25519_MLKEM768_new(void);"
.br
.BI "void PQBLOCKS_KEM_X25519_MLKEM768_free(PQBLOCKS_KEM_X25519_MLKEM768 *" kem ");"
.br
.BI "int PQBLOCKS_KEM_X25519_MLKEM768_encaps(const PQBLOCKS_KEM_X25519_MLKEM768 *" kem ", uint8_t *" ciphertext ", size_t *" ciphertext_len ", uint8_t *" shared_secret ", size_t *" shared_secret_len ", char **" envelope_json ");"
.br
.BI "int PQBLOCKS_KEM_X25519_MLKEM768_decaps(const PQBLOCKS_KEM_X25519_MLKEM768 *" kem ", const uint8_t *" ciphertext ", size_t " ciphertext_len ", const char *" envelope_json ", uint8_t *" shared_secret ", size_t *" shared_secret_len ");"
.PP
.BI "PQBLOCKS_SIG_ED25519_MLDSA65 *PQBLOCKS_SIG_ED25519_MLDSA65_new(void);"
.br
.BI "void PQBLOCKS_SIG_ED25519_MLDSA65_free(PQBLOCKS_SIG_ED25519_MLDSA65 *" sig ");"
.br
.BI "int PQBLOCKS_SIG_ED25519_MLDSA65_sign(const PQBLOCKS_SIG_ED25519_MLDSA65 *" sig ", const uint8_t *" message ", size_t " message_len ", uint8_t *" signature ", size_t *" signature_len ", char **" envelope_json ");"
.br
.BI "int PQBLOCKS_SIG_ED25519_MLDSA65_verify(const PQBLOCKS_SIG_ED25519_MLDSA65 *" sig ", const uint8_t *" message ", size_t " message_len ", const uint8_t *" signature ", size_t " signature_len ", const char *" envelope_json ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The PQBlocks hybrid C API implements misuse-resistant wrappers around post-quantum and classical algorithms.
.PP
All key encapsulation uses ML-KEM-768 with X25519, combining shared secrets with HKDF-SHA256 and enforcing HMAC-SHA256 key confirmation.
.PP
All digital signatures use ML-DSA-65 with Ed25519 in a dual composite envelope.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Functions return 0 (\fBPQBLOCKS_SUCCESS\fR) on success, or a negative error code on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pqblocks (3),
.BR pqblocks_policy (5)
